# q5_replica
Task 5.2  one NFS server against three HDFS replicas
20000 reads, node down with probability 0.5% per request, 8 ms per attempt

design            | available | mean   | p50    | p95
------------------+-----------+--------+--------+-------
one NFS server    |  99.485%  |  8.99  |  8.99  |  9.90 ms
3 replicas (HDFS) |  100.000%  |  9.04  |  9.01  |  9.91 ms

replica fetches attempted: 20101 for 20000 reads (1.005 per read)

storage and cost for 20 TB of data
  one copy  :  20.0 TB, 400 USD per month
  three copies:  60.0 TB, 1200 USD per month, 200% more storage

consistency
  asynchronous replica: 424 of 20000 reads (2.1%) could return old data
  synchronous replica : 0 stale reads, but every write waits for the
  slowest copy, so writes are slower and an unreachable copy can
  block the writer (the CAP trade-off).
